---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';

type Election = { year: number; ballots: number; native_local_reporting_units: number;
	native_unit_contest_vectors: number; native_contests: number; local_report_clock: string;
	county_report_clock: string; status: string };
type Contest = { year: number; native_contest: string; county_ballots: number;
	candidate_votes: number; unclassified_ballot_minus_contest_votes: number;
	two_party_margin_pp: number; candidates: { native_label: string; votes: number }[] };
type Comparison = { baseline_contest: string; two_party_margin_change_pp: number };
type Asset = { file: string; url: string; bytes: number; sha256: string };
const data = 'data/participation-columbia-wisconsin-history/20261107-01';
const history: { elections: Election[]; contest_context: Contest[]; descriptive_comparisons: Comparison[];
	reported_ballot_count_change_2026_minus_2024: number } =
	JSON.parse(readFileSync(`${data}/output/history.json`, 'utf8'));
const receipt: { assets: Asset[] } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(
	'public/participation-columbia-wisconsin-history/20261107-01/download.json', 'utf8'));
const sources: { elections: { source_receipts: { requested_url: string }[] }[] } =
	JSON.parse(readFileSync(`${data}/selected-observations.json`, 'utf8'));
const number = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US');
const signed = (value: number, precision = 0) => `${value > 0 ? '+' : ''}${value.toLocaleString('en-US',
	{ minimumFractionDigits: precision, maximumFractionDigits: precision })}`;
const fields = ['ballots', 'native_local_reporting_units', 'native_unit_contest_vectors', 'native_contests'] as const;
const contextFields = ['county_ballots', 'candidate_votes', 'unclassified_ballot_minus_contest_votes', 'two_party_margin_pp'] as const;
const labels: Record<string, string> = {
	'complete-analysis.zip': 'Complete Columbia inputs + code + tests + results (ZIP)',
	'native-ballots.csv': 'Every selected native ballot count (CSV)',
	'native-contest-vectors.csv': 'All selected contest and candidate counts (CSV)',
};
---

<section id="participation-columbia-wisconsin-history" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="columbia-wisconsin-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">County participation · presidential and midterm context</p>
		<h2 id="columbia-wisconsin-title">Columbia County, Wisconsin, 2024–2026</h2>
		<p>Two complete sets of native local and county reports.
			<strong>Both elections are unofficial snapshots here.</strong>
			Reported ballots fell by 7,725; that is <strong>not measured prior-voter drop-off</strong>,
			individual switching or demographic turnout.</p>
	</header>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Columbia Wisconsin reported participation counts">
		<table>
			<caption>Native ballot counts, not candidate votes or registered-voter turnout rates.
				Local units are municipalities or grouped wards, not 37 proven individual precincts.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Election</th><th scope="col">Reported ballots</th>
				<th scope="col">Native local units</th><th scope="col">Local contest vectors</th>
				<th scope="col">County contests</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>{history.elections.map(row => <tr data-columbia-year={row.year}>
				<th scope="row">{row.year} unofficial</th>
				{fields.map(field => <td data-columbia-field={field}>{number(row[field])}</td>)}
			</tr>)}</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p>2026 minus 2024 reported ballots:
		<strong data-columbia-ballot-change>{signed(history.reported_ballot_count_change_2026_minus_2024)}</strong>.
		{' '}Different election electorates are not a fixed-person cohort. No registration denominator,
		eligible-population rate, unique-person N26 or demographic denominator is qualified.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes" id="columbia-wisconsin-contests">
		<summary>Separate whole-county presidential and House context, not individual persuasion</summary>
		<p>Each displayed contest covers all 37 native units in its own election. Two-party margin is
			100 × (Democratic − Republican votes) / (Democratic + Republican votes).
			All literal parties and write-ins remain; independents are not reassigned.
			Ballot-minus-contest-vote gaps stay <strong>unclassified</strong>, not measured abstention,
			rejected ballots or missing voters.</p>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Columbia Wisconsin separate whole-county contests">
			<table>
				<caption>Presidential-to-House and House-to-House comparisons are separate context, not additive effects.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Contest</th><th scope="col">Reported ballots</th>
					<th scope="col">All candidate votes</th><th scope="col">Unclassified gap</th>
					<th scope="col">D minus R, two-party pp</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{history.contest_context.map((row, index) => <tr data-columbia-contest={index}>
					<th scope="row">{row.year} {row.native_contest}</th>
					{contextFields.map(field => <td data-columbia-field={field}>
						{field === 'two_party_margin_pp' ? signed(row[field], 2) : number(row[field])}
					</td>)}
				</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		{history.descriptive_comparisons.map((row, index) => <p>
			2024 {row.baseline_contest} to 2026 House 6:
			<strong data-columbia-margin-change={index}>{signed(row.two_party_margin_change_pp, 2)} pp</strong>
			{' '}in the county two-party margin, not an estimated share of persuasion or turnout effects.
		</p>)}
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Columbia Wisconsin every literal candidate">
			<table>
				<caption>All candidates and write-ins in the three displayed contests; every local contest remains in the complete download.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Election / contest / native candidate</th><th scope="col">Candidate votes</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{history.contest_context.map((contest, index) => contest.candidates.map((candidate, answer) =>
					<tr data-columbia-candidate={`${index}-${answer}`}>
						<th scope="row">{contest.year} {contest.native_contest}: {candidate.native_label}</th>
						<td data-columbia-field="votes">{number(candidate.votes)}</td>
					</tr>))}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>
	<details class="explorer-notes" id="columbia-wisconsin-methods">
		<summary>Four separate source clocks, coverage and complete reproducibility</summary>
		{history.elections.map((row, index) => <p data-columbia-clock={row.year}>
			<a href={sources.elections[index].source_receipts[0].requested_url}>Columbia County {row.year} archive</a>:
			{' '}local report {row.local_report_clock}; separate county report {row.county_report_clock}.
			{' '}Both say “{row.status}.” No timezone is supplied. Report footers, filenames,
			HTTP modification times and acquisition times are distinct.
		</p>)}
		<p>All 838 local contest vectors reconcile to 44 county contest controls.
			Matching unit names do not establish unchanged precinct boundaries or the same voters.
			No new longitudinal precinct map, individual transitions, original-coalition absence,
			new/returning-voter identity, demographic turnout, final-count certification or design confidence
			interval is inferred.</p>
		<p>The complete immutable ZIP contains every selected permitted factual input, all 76 ballot cells,
			2,647 candidate/answer cells, six sanitized original source receipts, methods, exact code,
			seven tests, complete CSVs and results, not metadata alone.
			Offline selected-fact reproduction does not rerun native PDF extraction or validate latent transitions.
			Native PDF/HTML, cookies and personal records are not redistributed.
			Selected governmental factual counts are not a native-document redistribution license.
			This analysis is not endorsed by the source.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		{receipt.assets.map(asset => <a href={asset.url} data-columbia-download={asset.file}>
			{labels[asset.file]}
		</a>)}
		<a href="/participation-columbia-wisconsin-history/20261107-01/download.json" download>Immutable download bytes + SHA-256</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-columbia-wisconsin-history { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
</style>
